  <static seed="84" source="Library/Michigan/Chap3Sec1/Q53.pg">
    <statement><p>Find an equation for the line tangent to the graph of <m>f</m> at
<m>(3,68)</m>, where <m>f</m> is given by
<m>f(x)= 3x^{3}-3x^{2}+14</m>.</p>
<p><m>y =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>63\mathopen{}\left(x-3\right)+68</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f'(x) =  9x^{2}-6x</m>, so
<m>f'(3) = 63</m>.  Thus the equation of the tangent line is 
<m>y - 68 = 63 ( x - 3 )</m>, or
<m>y = 68 + 63 (x - 3 )</m>.



</solution>
